---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { webSiteJsonLd, localBusinessJsonLd, buildFaqPageJsonLd } from "../../lib/seo";

const fitItems = [
  "You are behind or worried you may fall behind on mortgage payments",
  "The mortgage balance makes a normal cash sale hard to structure",
  "You want to move without bringing money to closing if the numbers allow",
  "You want a written comparison to review with family, partners, or advisors",
];

const safeguardItems = [
  "Payment expectations are written out before anything is signed",
  "Title, insurance, taxes, arrears, and lender deadlines are reviewed up front",
  "You can ask how payments will be verified each month",
  "We encourage attorney, CPA, lender, or housing counselor review before signing",
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What does a payment takeover option mean?",
    answer:
      "In some situations, ACE Properties KC may be able to buy the house while the existing loan stays in place and we step in to make the monthly payments. This is often called a subject-to structure and must be reviewed carefully.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can this help protect my credit?",
    answer:
      "It may help reduce further credit damage if it prevents additional missed payments or a completed foreclosure, but it does not erase late marks that already happened. Sellers should review credit, legal, and loan questions with qualified advisors.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is payment takeover right for every seller?",
    answer:
      "No. Loan terms, arrears, equity, deadlines, insurance, taxes, and seller risk all matter. We compare it with a cash offer and payoff-at-closing so you can decide what fits.",
  },
];

const jsonLd = [webSiteJsonLd(), localBusinessJsonLd(), buildFaqPageJsonLd(faqs)];
---

<Layout
  title="Cash or Payment Takeover Options | ACE Properties KC"
  description="Compare cash offers and payment takeover options for your Kansas City house, including subject-to structures for sellers behind on mortgage payments."
  canonicalPath="/options/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="section space-y-4">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-secondary">Your options</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold text-primary">Cash Offer or Payment Takeover Option</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">
      If the monthly mortgage payment is the pressure point, a straight cash offer is not always the only path. We can compare a clean as-is cash sale with creative options where we may be able to take over the payments, help catch up arrears, and give you a written plan to review before deciding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="card">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Cash Offer (As-Is)</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        Ideal when you want certainty and a quick exit. We purchase the property as-is, cover standard closing costs, and can close in as little as two weeks once title is ready.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-primary">
        <li>One walk-through, no open houses or repairs.</li>
        <li>Clear HUD/settlement statement before signing.</li>
        <li>Flexible closing date to match your move.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card bg-soft/80">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Payment Takeover Option</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        In some situations, we may be able to buy the house subject to the existing loan and step in to make the monthly payments for you. This can matter when you are behind, worried about foreclosure, or trying to move without bringing extra money to closing.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        A payment takeover can help reduce the pressure of missed payments and may help avoid the additional credit damage of a completed foreclosure, but it is not automatic and it is not right for every loan. Start with our <a href="/resources/subject-to-real-estate-kansas-city/" class="text-secondary underline">subject-to guide for Kansas City sellers</a> if this is the option you want to understand.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-primary">
        <li>We may take over the monthly mortgage payment if the structure fits.</li>
        <li>Arrears, taxes, insurance, and title items are reviewed up front.</li>
        <li>You receive the cash and creative options side by side.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-muted">
        Disclosure: Payment takeover and subject-to agreements can affect credit, taxes, insurance, and mortgage terms. Please consult your attorney, lender, CPA, or housing counselor before signing.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">When this is a fit</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-primary">
        {fitItems.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1 h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-secondary"></span>
            <span>{item}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="card space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Why sellers ask about payment takeover</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        The homeowner usually wants one simple thing: relief from the monthly payment. If a traditional cash offer cannot solve the payoff cleanly, we can review whether a subject-to or other creative structure gives you a better path.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        The goal is to stop guessing, see the numbers, and understand whether we can step in before the situation creates more stress or a completed foreclosure.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">How we keep the conversation careful</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-primary">
        {safeguardItems.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1 h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-secondary"></span>
            <span>{item}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="card space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Still deciding if as-is is right?</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        If repairs, clean-out, tenants, or timing are the main concern, our as-is selling guide explains how Kansas City sellers compare a direct offer against listing.
      </p>
      <a href="/resources/sell-house-as-is-kansas-city/" class="btn btn-ghost text-base">Read the as-is guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Want numbers for your property?</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        Share the address, rough mortgage balance, and what you are trying to solve. We can outline a cash offer, payment takeover option, or tell you when a traditional listing deserves a closer look.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        If you want to understand the offer assumptions first, read how <a href="/resources/how-cash-home-buyers-determine-offer-kansas-city/" class="text-secondary underline">cash home buyers determine an offer</a>.
      </p>
      <a href="/get-offer/" class="btn btn-primary text-base">Get an offer</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section flex flex-wrap gap-4">
    <a href="/get-offer/" class="btn btn-primary text-base">
      Start with the offer form
    </a>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-ghost text-base">
      Talk with us directly
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="section space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Payment takeover FAQ</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="card">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-primary">{faq.question}</summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{faq.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
